<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm in Drosophila eugracilis (Pass 2 sweep and controls) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "jacobian, turing_wavenumber and growth_rate are commented with the steady state and sigma(k). Lean theorems prove wavelength order, wavenumber reversal, twelve waves in 17820 nm, and the gamma order. The integer Lean wavelengths round the erecta float 2100.11 nm to 2100 nm." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm in Drosophila eugracilis (Pass 2 sweep and controls) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics, the Turing conditions, and k_c match the cited formulas. Self-test checks that the explicit dispersion and the 1/sqrt(gamma) shortcut agree to 1e-9, and that gamma=1 is exactly 1.485 µm. The length unit is assigned, not fitted to a species SEM, which is why this is not higher." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm in Drosophila eugracilis (Pass 2 sweep and controls) — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pearson r = 0.992 on six gamma points (reference 1, so the score is not self-referential). RMSE = 0.701 µm records the systematic FFT-versus-k_c offset instead of hiding it. KS luminance = 0.343. Blurred-arm fraction 0.177 versus raw Otsu 0.141. Focus spacing CV 0.294 versus a perfect lattice at 0. Absolute wavelength calibration remains biased; correlation does not remove that." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
